**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests`

**How to implement.** The tests' one door to the shipped catalogue (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; .spec-md §3.5): one fixture file compiled into both constructor suites by a link (AGENTS.md: share sources by file-linking). (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs`: `module BuiltinCatalogue` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, the FIRST `<Compile>` item of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, so every test file can open it. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` links it as its first `<Compile>` item, `<Compile Include="..\OpticalConstructor.Tests\BuiltinCatalogue.fs" Link="BuiltinCatalogue.fs" />`. No comment is added to either project file. (2) It loads the catalogue once per test process: a private `Lazy<CatalogueData>` over `(CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ()).readCatalogue ()` (step 38) that fails with the error's `describe` (step 39) on first use when the read fails, so no fact runs against a partial catalogue and a test run's start never throws. It exposes, each with a one-line doc: `catalogueData () : CatalogueData`; `freshStores () : InMemoryCatalogueStores`, new in-memory stores (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory`, step 40) filled by `importCatalogue` of the loaded catalogue and failing with the error's `describe` when the import is refused, isolated per call; the decoded entries of each kind in row order, `materials () : MaterialEntry list`, `categories () : MaterialCategory list`, `samples () : Sample list` and `presets () : LibraryEntry list` (sources, polarizers and detectors), which take the seed lists' place for the tests; and the lookups by well-known id, `material (id : MaterialId) : MaterialEntry`, `category (id : CategoryId) : MaterialCategory`, `sample (id : SampleId) : Sample` and `preset (id : ElementValueId) : LibraryEntry`, each failing with the id when the catalogue holds no such entry. Decoding uses step 25's decoders, and a decode failure fails with its `describe`. Nothing else is added: no write, no cache beyond the one load, no seed value. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.fs` (`module BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests`), appended to the compile list after `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs`. `the fixture's fresh stores hold the whole Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call`: the stores of one call list as many categories, materials, samples and presets as the fixture's lists, and removing `SampleIds.glassFilm600Id` from one call's samples leaves a second call's samples holding it. `the fixture resolves the built-ins by their well-known ids`: `material MaterialIds.silicon` is named `Silicon`, `category CategoryIds.vacuumCategory` is `HiddenOnCreate`, `sample SampleIds.multilayerQwId` is named `Quarter-wave glass/vacuum multilayer (41 layers)`, `preset PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer` is the `Ellipsometer` detector, and every entry of the four lists resolves through its own lookup to itself.

**Acceptance.** After the fixture lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the fixture's fresh stores hold the whole Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call` and `the fixture resolves the built-ins by their well-known ids`; `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` MUST compile `BuiltinCatalogue.fs` through its link, and ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.
